Every attempt is also saved in the app with its time and location. The photo, location and email are free.

**CrookCatcher Pro** adds **break-in detection**, which also takes a photo when someone gets the PIN wrong and then guesses it right, plus video with sound, a photo from the back camera, Google Drive backup, an alarm and a message on the lock screen.

CrookCatcher has been on Google Play since 2014, has been downloaded more than 12 million times and takes around 1.2 million intruder photos a day. Setup takes a few minutes and needs no account: see [how to see who tried to unlock your Android phone](/blog/see-who-tried-to-unlock-your-phone) for the steps.

